<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0637/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0637/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0637/>;
    dc:modified '2023-10-16T17:27:59'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'heat_flux_correction'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Flux correction is also called \'flux adjustment\'. A positive flux correction is downward i.e. added to the ocean. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0637'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0055/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0055/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0055/>;
    dc:modified '2023-10-16T17:23:18'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'water_flux_correction'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Water\' means water in all phases. Flux correction is also called \'flux adjustment\'. A positive flux correction is downward i.e. added to the ocean. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0055'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/0D56ZL18/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/0D56ZL18/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/0D56ZL18/>;
    dc:modified '2023-10-16T17:23:15'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'moles_of_dissolved_nitrogen_per_unit_mass_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The construction "moles_of_X_per_unit_mass_in_Y" is also called "molality" of X in Y, where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as "nitrogen" or a phrase such as "nox_expressed_as_nitrogen". "Dissolved nitrogen" means the sum of all nitrogen in solution: inorganic nitrogen (nitrite, nitrate and ammonium) plus nitrogen in carbon compounds.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::0D56ZL18'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/2NMYVULV/1/> .
