    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'mass_concentration_of_prokaryotes_expressed_as_carbon_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Mass concentration" means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction "mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as "nitrogen" or a phrase such as "nox_expressed_as_nitrogen". The phrase "expressed_as" is used in the construction "A_expressed_as_B", where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. "Prokaryotes" means all Bacteria and Archaea excluding photosynthetic cyanobacteria such as Synechococcus and Prochlorococcus or other separately named components of the prokaryotic population.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::E16D9FIK'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/FK6NPY5L/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/FK6NPY5L/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/FK6NPY5L/>;
    dc:modified '2023-07-05T16:51:32'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'universal_thermal_climate_index'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Universal Thermal Comfort Index (UTCI) is an equivalent temperature of the actual thermal condition. Reference: utci.org. It is the air temperature of a reference condition causing the same dynamic physiological response in a human body considering its energy budget, physiology and clothing adaptation.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::FK6NPY5L'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/G0WQ5UB7/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/G0WQ5UB7/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/G0WQ5UB7/>;
    dc:modified '2023-07-05T16:51:32'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'specific_enthalpy_of_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specific_enthalpy_of_air is the enthalpy of air per unit mass, which can be computed for an air sample as the sum of the enthalpy of the dry air and the enthalpy of the water vapor in that air, divided by the mass of dry air.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::G0WQ5UB7'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/H4NYWUZ1/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/H4NYWUZ1/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/H4NYWUZ1/>;
    dc:modified '2023-07-05T16:51:32'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'specific_turbulent_kinetic_energy_of_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Specific means per unit mass. "Turbulent kinetic energy" is the kinetic energy of all eddy-induced motion that is not resolved on the grid scale of the model.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::H4NYWUZ1'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/L7HK0CKS/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/L7HK0CKS/1/>
